   "note": "The authored key stands.  The stem asks for the three sentences showing the order closes on a MEASURED RESULT rather than on the work being finished, and the blind read swapped span 4 for span 2.  Span 2 is a scheduling fact, the date Dr. Kessler's next status log falls on, and says nothing about what closes the order;  span 4, that a clean panel is effort and a recovered reading is evidence, states the principle the whole item is about.  Span 3 was shortened in the 26-0822 prose pass, from 32 words to 26, and reworded from that log to that status log so it names its own referent rather than leaning on span 2 for it.  That change was made in response to this disagreement and did not move the blind read, which confirms the pull is the model under-weighting a principle sentence against a concrete one rather than an ambiguity in the text.",
